From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:29:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 115/138] skinny sm86 v2: row tiling for 33-64 rows + fused HC
 down/silu (VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86_HC=1)

- Grid (M tile, N tile, K split), M tiles fastest so programs sharing a W
  tile run together; split-K partials/counters per (M, N) tile. Plans can now
  cover 48/64 rows with 2-4 smaller tiles (W23: several 48/64-row shapes now
  beat cuBLAS; with realistic clocks cuBLAS stays competitive on others).
- VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86_HC=1: HyperConnection down projection applies hc_silu
  in its epilogue (rounds where the unfused op rounds: bit-exact, W23 hctest);
  GatedResidual._project routes through qwen4_exp_skinny_sm86_hc_down /
  _hc_up_mix. The fused up projection + gate mix kernel is kept but lost to
  skinny GEMM + hc_gate_mix at every M (walks the 4 streams serially), so no
  "mix:" plans: _hc_up_mix falls back to the skinny GEMM, then hc_gate_mix.
- VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86_HC registered as a compile factor.

W23 (plans-sm86-w23.json, tuned with idle gaps between replays: back-to-back
replays had throttled the 200 W-capped 3090s to ~330 MHz SM in W18):
greedy single code/prose/count 281.9/121.9/373.2 (p5 264.0/129.8/369.9,
p3b 241.8/112.2/335.3); unfused v2 275.6/115.3/371.9; stress 1000x PASS,
hctest PASS, probes 8/8 x2, NaN poke clean, GSM8K 97.0, 0 runtime errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
