+Y[M, N] = X[M, K] @ W[N, K]^T: one program per (M tile, N tile, K split),
+tensor-core dot with M padded to BLOCK_M. M tiles vary fastest in launch order,
+so the programs that share a W tile run together and all but the first read it
+from L2. With SPLIT_K > 1 every split stores an fp32 partial and the last split
+to arrive (per-tile counter) sums them in fixed order and resets the counter:
+deterministic, one launch. Every enabled layer owns its counters and partials
+(a "slot"), so layers on different streams never share them.
+
+VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86_HC=1 also fuses the HyperConnection chain around the two
+projections: the down projection applies hc_silu to its LoRA columns in the
+epilogue, and the up projection computes the sigmoid gate mix over the HC
+streams in its epilogue (block input instead of the [M, HC*H] gate). Both
+round exactly where the unfused ops round, so they match the unfused skinny
+path bit for bit.
 
 Plans are measured per local (N, K) shape and M bucket by
 /opt/flash-next/skinny/bench.py and read from VLLM_EXP_SKINNY_SM86_PLANS
-(JSON); shapes and M without a plan, and M > 64, keep F.linear.
+(JSON; "mix:NxK" keys are fused up-projection plans); shapes and M without a
+plan, and M > 64, keep F.linear (and the unfused HC ops).
